    ns75:StarShaclSchema dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.validator.StarShaclSchema" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """A SHACL schema: a bound shapes graph (``self.shacl_graph``) plus an
    optional ontology graph (``self.ont_graph``), each a reference to its
    own separate graph - this class does not itself *hold* triples the way
    ``StarLayerGraph`` does (composition, not inheritance: there's no real
    "is-a" relationship available between it and any existing rdflib/
    pyshacl class - pySHACL's own main entry point, ``validate()``, is a
    stateless one-shot function, not a long-lived object to subclass, and
    this class unifies several independent capabilities
    (``validate``/``apply_rules``/``evaluate``/``extract_subgraph``)
    rather than specializing any one of them). Construct one per distinct
    shapes-set (``PersonSchema = StarShaclSchema(person_shapes)``,
    ``ProductSchema = StarShaclSchema(product_shapes)``, ...), then call
    ``validate``/``apply_rules``/``evaluate``/``extract_subgraph`` against
    whatever data graph you're checking.

    Adds RDF 1.2/triple-term adaptation around pySHACL, which understands
    neither triple terms nor SHACL 1.2's own predicates natively.""" ;
        rdfs:label "StarShaclSchema" ;
        ns2:declares ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_shacl_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema.evaluate_component, ns75:StarShaclSchema.close_shape, ns75:StarShaclSchema.target_nodes, ns75:StarShaclSchema._ensure_native_component_shapes_typed, ns75:StarShaclSchema._try_native_structural_property_validation, ns75:StarShaclSchema._annotate_used_graphs_and_configuration, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_shapes_graph_and_provenance, ns75:StarShaclSchema.evaluate, ns75:StarShaclSchema._strip_deactivated_node_expressions, ns75:StarShaclSchema._try_native_literal_only_validation, ns75:StarShaclSchema.apply_rules, ns75:StarShaclSchema.validate, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_literal_only_component_name, ns75:StarShaclSchema._augment_shapes_with_new_target_types, ns75:StarShaclSchema._nodes_conforming_to, ns75:StarShaclSchema._annotate_conformance_disallows, ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__, ns75:StarShaclSchema._humanize_report_text, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_data_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema.build_report, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_structural_component_definition, ns75:StarShaclSchema.extract_subgraph, ns75:StarShaclSchema._try_native_core_validation, ns75:StarShaclSchema.extract_shapes_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema.validate_each ;
        ns2:filePath "/Users/johnclements/Documents/GitHub/hidden-graph/starlayer/packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/validator.py" ;
        ns2:lineEnd 2126 ;
        ns2:lineStart 80 .

    ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__ dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.validator.StarShaclSchema.__init__" ;
        a ns2:Method ;
        rdfs:comment """Bind a shapes graph (plus optional ontology/data graphs and an
    entailment regime) once, so every processing method
    (``validate``/``apply_rules``/``evaluate``/``extract_subgraph``/
    ``target_nodes``) can be called repeatedly without re-passing the
    same arguments.""" ;
        rdfs:label "__init__" ;
        ns2:filePath "/Users/johnclements/Documents/GitHub/hidden-graph/starlayer/packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/validator.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.shacl_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.data_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.validate_fn, ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.inference, ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.ont_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.adapter ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.returns ;
        ns2:isDunder true ;
        ns2:lineEnd 188 ;
        ns2:lineStart 100 ;
        ns2:signature "def __init__(self, shacl_graph: Any | None=None, ont_graph: Any | None=None, *, data_graph: Any | None=None, inference: Any | None=None, adapter: TripleTermAdapter | None=None, validate_fn: Callable[..., tuple[bool, Graph, str]] | None=None) -> None" .

    ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.adapter a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "Overrides the ``TripleTermAdapter`` used to encode/decode triple terms around pySHACL. Defaults to a fresh ``TripleTermAdapter()``." ;
        rdfs:label "adapter" ;
        ns2:annotationText "TripleTermAdapter | None" ;
        ns2:defaultValue "None" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:starlayer.shacl.adapters.TripleTermAdapter ;
        ns2:optional true ;
        ns2:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        ns2:position 4 .

    ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.data_graph a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "An optional default data graph, bound once here the same way ``shacl_graph``/``ont_graph`` already are, so a caller performing several different operations (``validate()``, ``apply_rules()``, ``evaluate()``, ...) against the same data doesn't have to keep re-passing it to every method call - each method's own ``data_graph`` parameter is optional, falling back to this one (see ``_resolve_data_graph()``). Still fully overridable per call - binding a default here doesn't prevent passing a different ``data_graph`` to any one method." ;
        rdfs:label "data_graph" ;
        ns2:annotationText "Any | None" ;
        ns2:defaultValue "None" ;
        ns2:hasType ns4:typing.Any ;
        ns2:optional true ;
        ns2:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        ns2:position 2 .

    ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__.param.inference a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "An optional entailment regime (one of the real ``ENTAILMENT.*`` IRIs, or an iterable of them), bound once here rather than accepted as a per-method keyword - an entailment regime is realistically a property of \"how this schema interprets its data,\" not something a caller would want to vary call-to-call on the same schema. Methods below don't accept their own ``inference=`` parameter at all - construct a second ``StarShaclSchema`` with a different ``inference=`` if two different regimes are genuinely needed against the same shapes/data." ;
        rdfs:label "inference" ;
